# Design Tokens & UI Parity

## Source of truth

- **Figma:** [TTW-Site](https://www.figma.com/design/9xmldPK4dDKp72K3oE7tcA/TTW-Site)
- **Code:** `packages/config/theme.css` — shared Tailwind v4 `@theme` tokens consumed by `web`, `app`, and `admin`.

## Rules

1. **Use tokens only.** Do not hardcode colors, font sizes, or spacing. Use Tailwind classes that map to the shared theme (e.g. `text-primary-600`, `bg-background`, `p-4`, `rounded-lg`, `font-sans`).
2. **Design parity.** Do not redesign; implement the approved Figma screens. Only small feasibility tweaks (responsive spacing, truncation) are allowed without changing intent.
3. **Adding tokens.** New colors, radii, or typography must be added to `packages/config/theme.css` and aligned with Figma. Document in `docs/design-rules.md` if you introduce new token names or scales.
4. **Semantic over raw.** Prefer semantic tokens where defined (e.g. `primary`, `background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `success`, `warning`, `error`) so theme updates propagate.

